  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\n- `.github/workflows/release.yml`: the existing `workflow_dispatch` gets a boolean input `site_only` (default `false`).\r\n  - `linux`, `macos`, `windows` and `wasm` have `if: ${{ !inputs.site_only }}`. `aur`, `snap` and `flatpak` need `linux`, so they are skipped too.\r\n  - `publish` stays tag-only. Its condition also has `!inputs.site_only`, so a `site_only` run never publishes.\r\n  - `site` is not changed. It builds from the dispatched ref and reads the version from that tree's `Cargo.toml` (0.25.0 on `site/v0.25.0`). With `wasm` skipped, app/ is the \"not part of this copy\" page, as for a failed wasm build.\r\n  - `pages` deploys on the tag path as before. It also deploys on a `site_only` dispatch, but only from a `site/*` branch.\r\n- `xtask/tests/release_site_tests.rs`: the new test `site_only_dispatch_runs_only_site_and_pages` pins the triggers, the input and each job condition, `publish` included.\r\n- `docs/decisions/3276-site-redeploy.md`: the decision, the dropped options and the owner action.\r\n\r\n## Why it is safe\r\n\r\n- No new trigger. The triggers are still the `vX.Y.0` tag push and `workflow_dispatch` (the test pins the list).\r\n- No fork path. Only a collaborator can dispatch a workflow. All jobs are GitHub-hosted.\r\n- `publish` is still tag-only and skips on `site_only`. A `site_only` run cannot make a release page.\r\n- The tag path and the plain dispatch path keep their behaviour: `inputs.site_only` is empty on a push and `false` by default.\r\n- A `site_only` dispatch from `main` builds the site as a check and does not deploy it.\r\n\r\n## Test run\r\n\r\n- `CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1 cargo test -p xtask --test release_site_tests`: 2 passed.\r\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --test release_site_tests -- -D warnings`: clean.\r\n- The YAML parses (`yaml.safe_load`), and the job conditions read as above.\r\n- The branch `site/v0.25.0` (site fixes at `3bc320a8c`) passes `python -m unittest discover -s site/tests`: 82 tests OK.\r\n\r\n## The same release.yml goes on site/v0.25.0 before the dispatch\r\n\r\nGitHub runs a dispatch with the workflow file of the dispatched ref. The tag's `release.yml` has no `site_only` input. Thus `site/v0.25.0` has the `release.yml` of this PR as one commit, `ci(release): site_only dispatch (from PR #3277)` (head `e41d7129f`). That file is byte-identical to the file at this PR's head `b05a95c39`. If this PR changes `release.yml` again, the same file goes on `site/v0.25.0` again before the dispatch.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- No workflow ran. The dispatch is still owed:\r\n  `gh workflow run release.yml --ref site/v0.25.0 -f site_only=true`\r\n- Owner action first: the `github-pages` environment must permit the branch policy `site/*`. Without it, GitHub refuses the `pages` deploy of the dispatch.\r\n\r\nChangelog: none\r\nProcess change: yes\r\nEffort: medium\r\n\r\nRefs #3276\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n",
